--
N5008 [class.member.lookup]/3: outside a complete-class context the search
for a name is from its point of use, so the constructor's parameter
`const month_day_last &' names the class, not the member function
month_day_last() declared after it.  The front end type-checks constructors
after all other members (typecheck_compound_body) and found the member
function ("found no match for symbol 'month_day_last'", bin53); a
constructor parameter's unqualified class name is now resolved at the
constructor's position (pin_constructor_parameter_class_names).  Reduced
(cvise, /tmp/r163/red/kb_V_chrono_c) from libc++ 18's
chrono::year_month_day_last, whose operator+= and friends were dropped
(cpp20_libcxx_header_drops/test_chrono.desc).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept
this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
